{"id":938,"date":"2020-11-12T12:50:59","date_gmt":"2020-11-12T20:50:59","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=938"},"modified":"2024-09-01T20:09:50","modified_gmt":"2024-09-02T03:09:50","slug":"codrone-arduino-updating","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-updating\/","title":{"rendered":"Updating CoDrone"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ae6e46d\" name=\"6a2215ae6e46d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Updating CoDrone Library<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Open up Arduino and go to Sketch &gt; Include Library &gt; Manage Libraries\u2026[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;939&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]In the Library Manager window that appears, search for CoDrone in the search box located at the top right.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;940&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]CoDrone by Robolink should appear.\u00a0If you do not see the CoDrone library,\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/en\/Main\/Software\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">update your Arduino IDE.<\/a> Select the library and update.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;941&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ae6e580\" name=\"6a2215ae6e580\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Updating board files<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Open Arduino and navigate to Tools &gt; Boards &gt; Boards Manager.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;942&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]In the Type<strong>\u00a0<\/strong>box, change the type from All to Contributed.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;943&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Find the package rokit by ROBOLINK. Click anywhere in the box and then click the Update button.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;944&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>You\u2019re done! Your Rokit Smart Inventor Board files are now up to date!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 3 Updating CoDrone Library [vc_column_text]Open up Arduino and go to Sketch &gt; Include Library &gt; Manage Libraries\u2026[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=\"939\" img_size=\"large\" alignment=\"center\"][vc_column_text]In the Library Manager window that appears, search for&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-updating\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1752,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2163,2164,2165,2169,2178],"class_list":["post-938","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-software","lesson-tag-update","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/938","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolin